From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:59:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: cpif: shm_ipc: index regions by their
 memory-region position

Stock gives each of the modem's reserved-memory nodes an "rmem_index"
property, and shm_ipc fails without it. Those are generic
reserved-memory nodes here, shared with nothing but still not the place
for a driver's numbering. Use the position in the shared-memory node's
memory-region list when the property is absent (stock lists them in
index order, so the result is the same), and drop the node references.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/cpif/shm_ipc.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/shm_ipc.c b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/shm_ipc.c
index 92dc13e50..66b23a49c 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/shm_ipc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/shm_ipc.c
@@ -45,9 +45,15 @@ static int cp_rmem_setup_latecall(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		if (!np)
 			break;
 
-		mif_dt_read_u32(np, "rmem_index", rmem_index);
+		/*
+		 * Stock gives each reserved-memory node an "rmem_index";
+		 * without one, the position in memory-region is the index.
+		 */
+		rmem_index = i;
+		mif_dt_read_u32_noerr(np, "rmem_index", rmem_index);
 
 		rmem = of_reserved_mem_lookup(np);
+		of_node_put(np);
 		if (!rmem) {
 			mif_err("of_reserved_mem_lookup() failed\n");
 			break;
